language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ dudeney_numbers: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A Dudeney Number is a positive integer that is a perfect cube such that the sum of its digits is equal to the cube root of the number. Find such a number that is also larger than 1 and has at most n digits.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `dudeney_numbers.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/dudeney_numbers.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `dudeney_numbers_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py dudeney_numbers.json
$   savilerow model.eprime dudeney_numbers_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the largest number of digits allowed (at most 10 in this model)
given n : int(1..10)

$ number: the Dudeney number found (the output): a perfect cube larger than 1 with at most n digits
find number : int(2..10**n-1)
$ root: the cube root of number, which equals the sum of its at most n digits, so at most 9 * n
find root : int(2..9 * n)
$ digits[k]: digit k of number, indices 1-based with digit 1 the units digit
find digits : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..9)

branching on [root]
such that
$ the number is a perfect cube: it is the cube of its root
number = root * root * root,
$ the digits of the number, weighted by their place value, make up the number
number = (sum k : int(1..n) . digits[k] * 10**(k-1)),
$ the sum of the digits of the number is equal to its cube root
root = (sum k : int(1..n) . digits[k])
